### Describe the problem

Our team is using the `convertFileSrc` to show some pictures in local storage, but sometimes our team members may make mistakes. For example, somebody has already converted the url in his field, but another one calls `convertFileSrc` again before displaying the image.

The final url may looks like `asset://asset%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%2F%252FUsers%252Fczf%252FDesktop%252F1.jpg`. It will lead to some bugs and it is a little bit hard to fix because you don't know where and when they call the `convertFileSrc`. This is a really big trouble in our team.

### Describe the solution you'd like

To fix this problem, we encapsulated some functions to avoid calling `convertFileSrc` twice. By the way, we also provide a function to convert the url back to the raw file path.

``` typescript
import { convertFileSrc } from '@tauri-apps/api/tauri'
import { type, OsType } from '@tauri-apps/api/os';

// it will store the conversion result
const urlMap = new Map<string, string>();

/**
 * convert the asset url back to file path
 * @param url tauri asset url
 * @returns file path, it may not exist if it is not converted before.
 */
export function urlConvertToPath(url: string): string | undefined {
    return urlMap.get(url);
}

// to avoid repeated `if` statements, we use a variable to store the judgement function
let osType: OsType | null = null;
let checkIfConverted: (path: string) => boolean;

export async function pathConvertToUrl(path: string): Promise<string> {
    // this statement will be optimized when osType is configured, so it will not have drawbacks in performance
    if (!osType) {
        osType = await type();

        if (osType === "Windows_NT") {
            checkIfConverted = (path: string) => {
                return path.startsWith("https://asset.localhost/");
            }
        } else {
            checkIfConverted = (path: string) => {
                return path.startsWith("asset://localhost/");
            }
        }
    }

    // avoid double conversion
    if (checkIfConverted(path)) {
        return path;
    }

    // store the conversion result in Map, so you can convert is back to file path through this Map
    const url = convertFileSrc(path);
    urlMap.set(url, path);
    return url;
}
```

